 "lines": [
  {
   "text": "Otto's crackers puffed up like pillows. His mouse moved into one.",
   "s": 0.12,
   "e": 3.513
  },
  {
   "text": "Otto had banned the little holes. \"Holes are lazy!\" So why do crackers have holes?",
   "s": 3.713,
   "e": 7.55
  },
  {
   "text": "Day one, the crackers came out round as hamburger buns. Otto called them \"fluffy.\"",
   "s": 7.85,
   "e": 11.905
  },
  {
   "text": "Day two, they swelled like beach balls. One rolled out and chased the mailman.",
   "s": 12.025,
   "e": 15.579
  },
  {
   "text": "Nibbles the mouse was furious. His cracker house used the holes as windows.",
   "s": 15.779,
   "e": 19.608
  },
  {
   "text": "So Otto stacked bricks on the oven door. \"Holes are lazy!\"",
   "s": 19.808,
   "e": 22.869
  },
  {
   "text": "At noon, the door blew open and shot four hundred crackers over Crumbleton, like popcorn.",
   "s": 22.989,
   "e": 26.411
  },
  {
   "text": "So what are the holes for?",
   "s": 26.611,
   "e": 27.576
  },
  {
   "text": "Dough is wet. In the oven, that water turns to steam, and steam wants out.",
   "s": 27.876,
   "e": 31.225
  },
  {
   "text": "The holes are tiny chimneys. Steam escapes, so the cracker bakes flat and crisp.",
   "s": 31.625,
   "e": 35.589
  },
  {
   "text": "Otto put the holes back. \"Holes are lazy,\" he says. \"So I gave them a job.\"",
   "s": 35.789,
   "e": 39.82
  },
  {
   "text": "Nibbles got his windows back. The mailman still runs past the bakery.",
   "s": 39.94,
   "e": 43.6
  }
 ],
